id: 20
hanzi: 胆小鬼
pinyin: dǎn xiǎo guǐ
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: coward; craven person; chicken
  es: cobarde; gallina; pusilánime; miedica

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a person who utterly lacks courage, is easily frightened, or shrinks from difficulty or danger | persona timorata que carece de valor, se asusta fácilmente o huye ante el peligro | 骂他是胆小鬼 (call him a coward)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 秦军为了激怒赵括出战，故意派人在营垒前大声嘲笑他是只敢缩在堡垒里的胆小鬼。 | Qínjūn wèile jìnù Zhào Kuò chūzhàn, gùyì pài rén zài yínglěi qián dàshēng cháoxiào tā shì zhǐ gǎn suō zài bǎolěi lǐ de dǎnxiǎoguǐ. | To provoke Zhao Kuo into combat, Qin deliberately sent men to laugh outside his camp, taunting him as a coward hiding in bastions. | Para provocar la furia de Zhao Kuo, Qin envió emisarios a mofarse de él llamándole cobarde refugiado tras las murallas.
  #2 | 面对突如其来的危急关头，真正的勇士绝不做临阵脱逃的胆小鬼，而是挺身而出勇挑重担。 | Miànduì tūrúqílái de wēijí guāntóu, zhēnzhèng de yǒngshì jué bù zuò línzhèn-tuōtáo de dǎnxiǎoguǐ, ér shì tǐngshēn'érchū yǒng tiāo zhòngdàn. | Facing sudden peril, true warriors never act as cowards fleeing from battle; instead, they step forward bravely to shoulder burdens. | Ante la adversidad repentina, el verdadero valiente rehúsa ser un cobarde que deserte; da un paso al frente asumiendo el deber.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  做胆小鬼 | be / act like a coward
  不是胆小鬼 | not a coward
  嘲笑胆小鬼 | mock someone as a coward
  胆小鬼行为 | cowardly behavior
  被称为胆小鬼 | be called a coward
  胆小怕事 | timid and cowardly afraid of trouble

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  胆小如鼠 | dǎn xiǎo rú shǔ | as timid as a mouse; gutless
  贪生怕死 | tān shēng pà sǐ | craving life and fearing death; cowardly
  胆大包天 | dǎn dà bāo tiān | audacious enough to cover the sky; bold and daring (antonym)
  视死如归 | shì sǐ rú guī | look upon death as going home; fearless hero

character_decomposition[3]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  胆 | dǎn | gallbladder; courage; guts; bravery | vesícula biliar; valor; agallas; coraje | 月 | flesh / organ | 月/肉 (flesh / internal organ) + 旦 (dawn rising sun) | 旦 (dàn) | 9 | 左右结构 | The bodily internal organ 月 that generates resolute courage like the rising morning sun 旦. | An internal organ (月) radiating courage and boldness like the dawn sun (旦) to form guts (胆). | Una entraña vital (月) que irradia valentía al nacer el sol (旦), sede del coraje (胆). | 214 | BAM | 膽
  小 | xiǎo | small; tiny; little; young | pequeño; diminuto; menor | 小 | small | a vertical object split in half into tiny flecks | 小 (xiǎo) | 3 | 单一结构 | A vertical mark divided into two tiny side specks; indicates smallness. | Dividing a small stone into tiny flecks (小). | Partir una pequeña piedra en diminutas esquirlas (小). | 214 | NC | 小
  鬼 | guǐ | ghost; spirit; crafty person; fellow | fantasma; espectro; pillo; tipo | 鬼 | ghost | kneeling human figure with an oversized eerie mask/skull | 鬼 (guǐ) | 9 | 单一结构 | A spirit or human wearing an uncanny skull-like head mask; used colloquially for a specific type of person. | A figure with a mask scurrying in the shadows like an eerie apparition (鬼). | Una silueta enmascarada que se escurre en la penumbra espectral (鬼). | 214 | HUI | 鬼

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A person whose courage (胆) is minutely tiny (小) and acts like a skittish phantom (鬼) is a coward (胆小鬼).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Aquel cuyo coraje (胆) es diminuto (小) y huye como una sombra asustadiza (鬼) es un cobarde (胆小鬼).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Traditional Chinese medicine associates the gallbladder (胆) with decisiveness and bravery; '胆小' indicates faint-heartedness.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Third tone sandhi chain: 'dǎn xiǎo guǐ' -> pronounced 'dán xiáo guǐ' (35-35-214). The first two syllables shift to second tone.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    但 | dàn | but; however | Person radical 亻 on left instead of 月
    少 | shǎo | few; little | Has downward right-slanting stroke across bottom
    魁 | kuí | chief; head | Dipper 斗 on right of 鬼
    魂 | hún | soul; spirit | Cloud 云 on left of 鬼
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    大胆 | dàdǎn | bold; audacious
    胆量 | dǎnliàng | courage; guts
    醉鬼 | zuìguǐ | drunkard
    机灵鬼 | jīlingguǐ | clever little rascal

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 胆小鬼 is an informal colloquial noun mocking someone who shrinks from fright or lacks fortitude.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 胆小鬼 vs. 勇士 | yǒngshì | 勇士 is the direct antonym meaning a brave, fearless warrior.
    2 | 胆小鬼 vs. 英雄 | yīngxióng | 英雄 is an admired heroic champion, opposite to craven 胆小鬼.
    3 | 胆小鬼 vs. 懦夫 | nuòfū | 懦夫 is formal literary for coward, whereas 胆小鬼 is the common spoken idiom.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在古代两军对垒中，如何激怒敌将是一门攻心战术。秦军在阵前高声讽刺赵括是“只配躲在营垒里喝稀饭的胆小鬼”。自幼心高气傲的赵括哪堪忍受这般当众羞辱，为了证明自己不是胆小鬼，他不顾一切地下令全军出击，最终惨败。 | Zài gǔdài liǎng jūn duìlěi zhōng, rúhé jìnù díjiàng shì yī mén gōngxīn zhànshù. Qínjūn zài zhènqián gāoshēng fěngcì Zhào Kuò shì 'zhǐ pèi duǒ zài yínglěi lǐ hē xīfàn de dǎnxiǎoguǐ'. Zìyòu xīngāo-qì'ào de Zhào Kuò nǎ kān rěnshòu zhè bān dāngzhòng xiūrǔ, wèile zhèngmíng zìjǐ bùshì dǎnxiǎoguǐ, tā bùgù-yīqiè de xiàlìng quán jūn chūjī, zuìzhōng cǎibài. | Provoking opposing generals was psychological warfare. Qin soldiers shouted that Zhao Kuo was a coward fit only to sip porridge in camp. Vain Zhao Kuo could not endure the humiliation; to prove he was no coward, he attacked and lost all. | En la guerra antigua, exasperar al general rival era un arte sutil. Qin gritaba que Zhao Kuo era un cobarde apto solo para tomar gachas en su tienda. El soberbio Zhao Kuo no soportó la afrenta; para demostrar su valor atacó y pereció.
  #2 | 面对生活中的挫折与困难，承认害怕并不等于就是懦弱的胆小鬼。真正的勇敢不是毫无畏惧，而是在内心感到恐惧时，依然选择直面风浪、坚定地迈开脚步向前探索。克服恐惧的过程，正是心灵由弱小走向强大的必经之路。 | Miànduì shēnghuó zhōng de cuòzhé yǔ kùnnan, chéngrèn hàipà bìng bù děngyú jiùshì nuòruò de dǎnxiǎoguǐ. Zhēnzhèng de yǒnggǎn bùshì háowú wèijù, ér shì zài nèixīn gǎndào kǒngjù shí, yīrán xuǎnzé zhímiàn fēnglàng, jiāndìng de màikāi jiǎobù xiàngqián tànsuǒ. Kèfú kǒngjù de guòchéng, zhèngshì xīnlíng yóu ruòxiǎo zǒuxiàng qiángdà de bìjīng zhī lù. | Admitting fear before life's setbacks does not make one a coward. True bravery is not the absence of fear, but pressing forward into the storm despite fear. Conquering terror is how the soul matures from frailty into strength. | Reconocer el temor ante la adversidad no nos convierte en cobardes. El auténtico coraje no estriba en no sentir miedo, sino en marchar hacia la tempestad a pesar del pánico; vencer el recelo transforma la flaqueza en entereza.
